# Environment for working on culm itself. Copy it, then fill in what you need:
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# culm does not read .env on its own; load it into your shell first:
#
#   set -a && . ./.env && set +a
#
# Every variable is optional. A commented-out line is unset; uncomment it to
# use it. An empty `NAME=` is NOT the same as unset: it still sets the
# variable, so an empty NO_COLOR hides the banner and an empty endpoint
# breaks telemetry. .env is gitignored; never commit a real token.

# === culm

# Telemetry is off by default. 1, true, on, or yes opts in; anything else,
# or unset, keeps it off.
CULM_TELEMETRY=0

# Where opted-in telemetry is sent. Leave commented out for culm's default.
# Set it to test a receiver, such as your own telemetry/worker deployment.
# CULM_TELEMETRY_ENDPOINT=https://culm-telemetry.<your-subdomain>.workers.dev/events

# Any value hides the start-up banner. NO_COLOR does the same.
# CULM_NO_BANNER=1
# NO_COLOR=1

# === Releasing

# A crates.io API token with publish-new and publish-update scopes, from
# https://crates.io/settings/tokens. cargo publish reads it instead of
# needing cargo login. Only needed by whoever publishes releases.
# CARGO_REGISTRY_TOKEN=
